{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791623937,"nonce":"HCh8vyN2o7OewoEZsktskA2rGsA=","title":"Float pushed into an Array\u003cAny\u003e that holds Ints stores raw f64 bits","message":"Conformance row Issue10124 (test2). `var arr = [1,3,4]` is Array\u003cInt\u003e; passed to\n`addFloat(arr:Array\u003cAny\u003e, ...values:Float)`, `arr.push(v)` stores the f64 bit pattern\n(`bitcast f64 to i64` + `array_push`). Std.string then prints\n`[1,3,4,4617315517961601024,...]` instead of `[1,3,4,5,6,7]`.\n\nNot specific to inline/rest/using: a plain `addOne(arr:Array\u003cAny\u003e, v:Float)` given an\nArray\u003cInt\u003e fails the same way. HaxeArray carries no element-kind tag at run time, so the\ncallee cannot know what the array stores.\n\nRejected: storing a whole-number Float pushed into Any as Int. Raw f64 bits in\nArray\u003cDynamic\u003e are relied on (`args.push(2.0); Reflect.callMethod(null, f, args)` with\n`f(x:Float)` works today and would break).\n\nProposed (hxcpp-like):\n1. Runtime: a HaxeArray.flags bit HAXE_ARRAY_INT_ELEMS and `haxe_array_push_any_f64`\n   that stores `f as i64` when set (register_symbol! it).\n2. Push site: a Float push onto an Array\u003cAny\u003e/Array\u003cDynamic\u003e receiver calls the helper\n   (today array_push in stdlib/runtime_mapping.rs -\u003e build_array_push in stdlib/array.rs).\n3. Caller side: set the bit when a static Array\u003cInt\u003e flows into an Array\u003cAny\u003e/Dynamic\n   parameter or variable.\nCost: non-zero flags disable inline stores for that array; check the flags paths in\nhaxe_sys.rs. Alternative: a uniform boxed representation for Any arrays (much larger).","files":null}]}